<title>INDIA: Indian air cargo demand expected up in road strike.</title>
<headline>Indian air cargo demand expected up in road strike.</headline>
<text>
<p>BOMBAY, March 30, Reuter - Demand for air cargo services is expected to increase significantly if truck unions go ahead with their national strike from 12:01 a.m. Tuesday (1830 GMT Monday), an Indian Airlines Corp cargo official said in Bombay on Saturday.</p>
<p>He said the airline had already been expecting an increase in traffic as it was the financial year end when many companies tried to use up their transport budgets.</p>
</text>
